{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isQueryNameChar\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isQueryNameChar</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt8\">UInt8</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks if a byte may appear unescaped in a query parameter name: `isQueryDataChar` without `=`,\nwhich would end the name.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isQueryNameChar","kind":"def","line":328,"name":"Std.Http.Internal.Char.isQueryNameChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Internal/Char.lean#L328-L334"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isQueryDataChar\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isQueryDataChar</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt8\">UInt8</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks if a byte is a valid character in a URI query parameter, excluding the pair separator `&`.\n\nInspired by `query = *( pchar / \"/\" / \"?\" )` from RFC 3986. `=` is allowed because a value may\ncontain it (`?a=b=c`); a parameter name ends at its first `=`, so a parsed name never contains one.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isQueryDataChar","kind":"def","line":318,"name":"Std.Http.Internal.Char.isQueryDataChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Internal/Char.lean#L318-L326"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isUserInfoChar\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isUserInfoChar</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt8\">UInt8</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks if a byte is a valid character in a URI userinfo component according to RFC 3986.\n`userinfo = *( unreserved/ sub-delims / \":\" )`\n\nNote: It avoids the pct-encoded of the original grammar because it is used with `Encoding.lean`\nthat provides it.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isUserInfoChar","kind":"def","line":307,"name":"Std.Http.Internal.Char.isUserInfoChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Internal/Char.lean#L307-L316"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isRequestTargetChar\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isRequestTargetChar</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt8\">UInt8</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks if a byte may appear in a request-target (RFC 9112 §3.2): a URI character of RFC 3986 other\nthan `#`, since no form of request-target has a fragment. `%` starts a `pct-encoded` triplet, and\n`[` and `]` enclose an IP-literal host.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isRequestTargetChar","kind":"def","line":298,"name":"Std.Http.Internal.Char.isRequestTargetChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Internal/Char.lean#L298-L305"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isFragmentChar\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isFragmentChar</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt8\">UInt8</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks if a byte is a valid character in a URI fragment component according to RFC 3986.\n`fragment = *( pchar / \"/\" / \"?\" )`","docLink":"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isFragmentChar","kind":"def","line":290,"name":"Std.Http.Internal.Char.isFragmentChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Internal/Char.lean#L290-L296"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isQueryChar\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isQueryChar</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt8\">UInt8</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks if a byte is a valid character in a URI query component according to RFC 3986.\n`query = *( pchar / \"/\" / \"?\" )`","docLink":"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isQueryChar","kind":"def","line":282,"name":"Std.Http.Internal.Char.isQueryChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Internal/Char.lean#L282-L288"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isPChar\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isPChar</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt8\">UInt8</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks if a byte is a valid path character (`pchar`) according to RFC 3986.\n`pchar = unreserved / pct-encoded / sub-delims / \":\" / \"@\"`\n\nNote: The percent-encoding (`pct-encoded`) is handled separately by `isEncodedChar`,\nso this predicate only covers the non-percent characters.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isPChar","kind":"def","line":271,"name":"Std.Http.Internal.Char.isPChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Internal/Char.lean#L271-L280"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isSubDelims\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isSubDelims</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt8\">UInt8</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks if a byte is a sub-delimiter character according to RFC 3986.\nSub-delimiters are: `!`, `$`, `&`, `'`, `(`, `)`, `*`, `+`, `,`, `;`, `=`.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isSubDelims","kind":"def","line":261,"name":"Std.Http.Internal.Char.isSubDelims","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Internal/Char.lean#L261-L269"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isUnreserved\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isUnreserved</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt8\">UInt8</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks if a byte is an unreserved character according to RFC 3986. Unreserved characters are:\nalphanumeric, hyphen, period, underscore, and tilde.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isUnreserved","kind":"def","line":252,"name":"Std.Http.Internal.Char.isUnreserved","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Internal/Char.lean#L252-L259"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isValidSchemeChar\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isValidSchemeChar</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks if a character is valid after the first character of a URI scheme.\nValid characters are ASCII alphanumeric, `+`, `-`, and `.`.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isValidSchemeChar","kind":"def","line":244,"name":"Std.Http.Internal.Char.isValidSchemeChar","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Internal/Char.lean#L244-L250"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/Char.html#Std.Http.Internal.Char.isAsciiAlphaNumChar\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Char</span>.<span class=\"name\">isAsciiAlphaNumChar</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Char\">Char</a>)